>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `prepare_rewrite_bundle`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments :
  simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> simpExtLib.simpset * thm list
simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle :
  simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle
simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle_rules : simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle ->
  (thm * simpExtLib.rewrite_source list) list
simpExtLib.combine_rewrite_bundles :
  simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle list -> simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle
simpExtLib.install_rewrite_bundle : simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle ->
  (simpExtLib.rewrite_source * thm) list ->
  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Prepares a theorem-list argument once, for use in several simplifier calls.

`prepare_rewrite_arguments ss ths` applies the directives in `ths` (such
as `simpExtLib.ExclX`, `SF` and `Split`) to `ss`, returning the resulting
simpset and the remaining theorems.

`prepare_rewrite_bundle ss ths` turns the theorems `ths`, which should
contain no directives, into rewrites using the rewrite maker of `ss`,
without adding them to `ss`. `install_rewrite_bundle bundle views ss` adds
them to `ss`, together with the views `views` (see
`simpExtLib.rewrite_views`). `rewrite_bundle_rules bundle` returns each
theorem of the bundle with the handles of the rewrites made from it.
`combine_rewrite_bundles` joins bundles.

The rewrites of a bundle are made only once: wherever it is installed,
bounded rewrites (`Once`, `Ntimes`) share one count of remaining uses.
`simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST_BOUND` takes a bundle already
installed in its simpset.

### Failure

`prepare_rewrite_arguments` fails if a directive fails.
`install_rewrite_bundle` fails if the bundle is already installed in the
simpset, and `combine_rewrite_bundles` if a bundle occurs twice. Views
whose source is not a rewrite of the bundle are ignored.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val (ss, ths) = simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments
     (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss)
     [BoundedRewrites.Once boolTheory.AND_CLAUSES];
>>_ val bundle = simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle ss ths;
>>_ val ss' = simpExtLib.install_rewrite_bundle bundle [] ss;
>> simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV ss' [] “T ∧ p”;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.rewrite_source_handles`](#simpExtLib.rewrite_source_handles),
[`simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC`](#simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC).
